From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ponwrt bring-up <noreply@example.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: allow NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED on Airoha

The Airoha AN7581 (EN7581) integrates a Wi-Fi Offload Engine that is the
same IP as the MediaTek MT7622 WED: both instances report
WED_REV = 0x76220001, and the WDMA cookie registers the vendor driver
writes (0x2a042a20 / 0x29002800, WDMA1 = +0x04000400) are bit-identical
to mainline's MT7622 v1 path in mtk_wed.c.

NET_VENDOR_MEDIATEK already accepts ARCH_AIROHA, but NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED
is gated on ARCH_MEDIATEK alone.  Without it every WED helper in
include/linux/soc/mediatek/mtk_wed.h compiles to its no-op stub, so
mt7915 never calls mtk_wed_device_attach() and the SoC-side ops table
that an external module installs is never consulted.

Allow ARCH_AIROHA as well.  Nothing is switched on by this change alone:
NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED is still def_bool NET_MEDIATEK_SOC != n, so it only
becomes y once NET_MEDIATEK_SOC is enabled, and on this platform the
mtk_eth_soc driver never probes (there is no mediatek,eth node), so
mtk_soc_wed_ops stays NULL and an external module can claim it safely.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Kconfig b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Kconfig
@@ -9,6 +9,6 @@ if NET_VENDOR_MEDIATEK
 
 config NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED
-	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK || ARCH_AIROHA || COMPILE_TEST
 	def_bool NET_MEDIATEK_SOC != n
 
 config NET_MEDIATEK_SOC

